course: dictionary
lesson: 13872
title: Kiddy and babyish words
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: A kiddy is a small child. Grown-ups often use it in a friendly way, like when they say, «The kiddies are playing in the garden.» Here kiddies means the little children.
explain: Kiddy can also describe things made for small children. «The kiddy pool was full of splashing toddlers» tells you the pool is for little ones. The clue is the word pool, not the child.
explain: Words can sound babyish. «That's a kiddy film!» could be said by an older child to show the film is too young for them. So the tone of the sentence matters as much as the meaning.
fact: Kiddy means a small child, and kiddie is another spelling of it.
fact: Kiddy is an informal word, so you would use it when talking with friends or family, not in a formal letter.
fact: As an adjective, kiddy means made for small children, as in «kiddy rides» or «the kiddy pool».
fact: Kiddy can be playful, as in «kiddy-winkies», a cheerful name for little children.
fact: Some older children feel kiddy sounds babyish, so they may tease with it, as in «That's a kiddy film!»
exercise: «The kiddy pool was shallow and warm.» What does kiddy mean here? | *Made for small children | Very deep and cold | Full of fish | For grown-ups only
exercise: «Oscar groaned, "That's a kiddy film!"» Why did Oscar groan? | *He felt the film was too babyish for him | He was asleep in his seat | He was too hot and tired | He had seen it three times and loved it
exercise: «The kiddies lined up for ice cream.» Find and copy one word that means small children. | lined | *kiddies | ice | cream
test: In which sentence does kiddy mean a small child? | "That's a kiddy film, not a real one." | *"The kiddy ran to find her mum." | "We bought a kiddy seat for the car." | "The kiddy pool was full of water."
test: Why might an older child say «That's a kiddy film!»? | To say the film is in another language | To say the film is very long | To ask for a ticket | *To suggest the film is babyish for their age
exam: Which best describes the word kiddy? | A scientific word for a machine | A name for a country | *Friendly, informal, and sometimes babyish | Old-fashioned and very formal
